[**Setting and Tone**:
setting(modern fantasy set in a world called Halphor. Halphor would look a lot like Earth to someone like you or me, but it has fantasy races and magic throughout it. Technology in Halphor is run with magic, rather than electricity. The story takes place in a country called Juhiro which shares superficial characteristics with Earth's modern Japan.)
genre(action + comedy + smut + romance + harem + slice of life)
]
[**{{user}}**:
backstory(At one point in time, {{user}} was widely known among ninjas as the most legendary majin hunter in the modern age under the title of "The Slayer". However, for reasons unknown to most, {{user}} ended their career early and now lives in a secluded dojo deep within Juhiro's mountains.
]
[**{{user}}'s Dojo**:
description({{user}}'s dojo is nestled on the side of a mountain and built around a natural hot springs. it is far away from civilization and most supplies are delivered there via post or grown there directly by {{user}}. Adjacent to the dojo is a small dorm where students reside, each with their own rooms and amenities, however, all bathing is done in the hot spring. The dojo also has a few underground sections that are home to obstacle courses and various training rooms for more intense training segments. A short walk away from the dojo is a waterfall pouring into a grotto, which is a common meditation spot for students.)
]

entries.content:
[**Majin**:
Majin are people who have made contracts with demons in order to gain magical power in exchange for their souls and often their servitude. They often have incredible magic power and require special training and aptitude to fight, conventional weapons are usually worthless against majin—unless infused with chakra. There are many shinobi organizations that seek to hunt and kill majin, often called "Majin Hunters". In order to maintain their contracts and gain even more power, majin are often required to make frequent ritualistic sacrifices by murdering other people. The process of forging a contract with a demon usually requires them to murder someone that is close to them.
]

[**Demon**:
Demons are extradimensional beings from the Spirit Realm that have no corporeal form in our world. They can't take tangible form in the Material World and only the most powerful of them can influence it in indirect ways. Some people are able to commune with demons, and might even form contracts with them, these individuals are called majin.
]

[**Spirit Realm**:
The Spirit Realm is an extradimensional world that overlaps with our own Material World. It is a world whose very shape and form is subject to those with enough willpower to mold it. The Spirit Realm is home to spirits, physical manifestations of emotions, concepts, and ideas. Benevolent Spirits are often called "archons", malevolent ones are "demons", and neutral-aligned spirits are just "spirits" or sometimes called "youkai". It is impossible for entities to cross the boundary between the Material World and the Spirit Realm, but spirits can still indirectly influence the Material World, and shinobi draw their power from the Spirit Realm in the form of Chakra to perform their techniques.
]

[**Shinobi**:
Shinobi are humanoids who utilize their innate chakra in order to perform superhuman tasks. They often do this to improve their agility, strength, endurance, and some (often called onmyo-nin or onmyoji) may even perform onmyo magic using chakra. One of the fundamental techniques of the shinobi is Chakra Armor, which is a ultra-hard invisible layer of chakra surrounding the entire body that most competent ninjas can maintain constantly.
]

[**Chakra Armor**:
Chakra armor is an ultra-thin, extremely dense layer of invisible chakra that shinobi can conjure to protect themselves. The armor has many benefits, primarily defensive in nature. It can easily protect a shinobi from damage and harm, being hard enough to ward off even blades and bullets; it is completely weightless and unrestrictive, meaning a shinobi can have their full range of motion and flexibility when summoning it; the shinobi can influence its appearance and how it looks to some degree (though it often takes forms and shapes that are revealing on women or extremely tight-fitting, nobody knows why); and in a pinch, the chakra that constitutes the armor can be used to fuel other techniques, though this is a risky maneuver as it requires the shinobi to summon more chakra armor afterward.
]

[**Majin Hunters**:
Majin hunters are shinobi whose job is to hunt and fight majin. They train specifically for this purpose, and that is their role in shinobi society. Many majin hunters have a "by any means necessary" mentality when hunting majins, but not all have such extreme mentalities.
]
